\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Changing the spin frame at each site}
\date{2026-11-23}

\p{A centered hop in direction #{j} acts on spin by
#{\varepsilon_j^S} and uses the [unitary link](fdip-009O) on
the internal fiber. Changing the spin frame at each site places
an inverse frame on the output and a frame on the input. If
the transformed spin factor is scalar, all spin components
see the same hop. Can the ordered Clifford generators furnish
such frames, including on the edge that closes a periodic row?}
